        "comments": "Due to the very large extent of repeats in this genome, a reassociation kinetics approach for partial genome sequencing was applied. Total Rhipicephalus microplus genomic DNA was prepared and processed by three Cot filtration experiments to enrich for single/low-copy and moderately repetitive DNAs. Cot-filtered DNA was sequenced using 454 FLX pyrosequencing. The filtered genomic DNA was de novo assembled. All contigs and BAC end sequences (GenBank Accession Numbers HN108288-HN118367) were then assembled with Cap3. WGS project ADMZ00000000 is the result of this two step assembly. In addition to these sequences, ten BACs (GenBank Accession Numbers HM748958-HM748967) were sequenced.",
